WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.067 --> 00:00:16.517
I still hadn't formulated a bubble bath soap for Mom or Tate.

2
00:00:16.518 --> 00:00:24.688
But after the disaster with Molly's bath soap, I decided I was finished with formulating them for now.

3
00:00:24.689 --> 00:00:30.377
As soon as Molly left, I went to my room to think.

4
00:00:30.378 --> 00:00:36.690
I started telling myself about all the great things I would invent someday.

5
00:00:36.691 --> 00:00:40.633
Soon I'd forgotten all about Molly's monster problem.

6
00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:46.777
That's when I got a fantastic idea, and I wasn't even trying!

7
00:00:46.778 --> 00:00:52.342
I ran into the kitchen and called Molly on the telephone.

8
00:00:52.343 --> 00:00:57.716
"When you go to bed, I want you to say something to yourself," I told her.

9
00:00:57.717 --> 00:01:00.967
She still sounded a little annoyed at me.

10
00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:04.813
"What should I say?" she asked.

11
00:01:04.814 --> 00:01:09.703
"You should say, 'I will not think of a monster ever, ever, ever.'

12
00:01:09.704 --> 00:01:12.505
Try it now," I coaxed her.

13
00:01:12.506 --> 00:01:18.878
"I will not think of a monster," repeated Molly. "Ever, ever, ever."

14
00:01:18.879 --> 00:01:23.267
"Good!" I said. "What are you thinking right now?"

15
00:01:23.268 --> 00:01:26.733
"I'm thinking of a monster," said Molly.

16
00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:29.049
"Argh!" I cried.

17
00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:32.500
"You're not supposed to think of a monster, Molly!"

18
00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:36.794
"Then stop reminding me, Iggy!" said Molly.

19
00:01:36.795 --> 00:01:41.281
I could tell my latest fantastic idea wasn't helping her much.

20
00:01:41.282 --> 00:01:45.655
I could also tell that Molly was really cranky from not sleeping.

21
00:01:45.656 --> 00:01:49.022
So we hung up a minute later.

22
00:01:49.023 --> 00:01:53.302
Guess what? That night I dreamed of a monster!

23
00:01:53.303 --> 00:01:55.850
It wasn't a scary monster though.

24
00:01:55.851 --> 00:01:58.978
It was a funny monster.

25
00:01:58.979 --> 00:02:03.479
Molly was late for school the next day because she had a dentist appointment.

26
00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:10.192
She came into the classroom just as Mrs. Romano was explaining our new project.

27
00:02:10.193 --> 00:02:15.384
I noticed Molly still looked tired, with dark circles under her eyes.

28
00:02:15.385 --> 00:02:22.214
"Today you will work with your partner and begin writing your books," Mrs. Romano was saying.

29
00:02:22.215 --> 00:02:27.717
"Will they be real books, like in a bookstore?" asked Ruby.

30
00:02:27.718 --> 00:02:33.651
"Your book will look like a real book when you are finished," said Mrs. Romano.

31
00:02:33.652 --> 00:02:37.046
"But it will not be sold in bookstores."

32
00:02:37.047 --> 00:02:39.812
Ruby looked disappointed.

33
00:02:39.813 --> 00:02:45.154
"Your books will be in the school library," Mrs. Romano went on.

34
00:02:45.155 --> 00:02:50.449
"Younger students can borrow them, so make sure you write a page-turner."

35
00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:52.682
Colby raised his hand.

36
00:02:52.683 --> 00:02:56.311
"What's a 'page-turner'?" he asked.

37
00:02:56.312 --> 00:02:58.433
Mrs. Romano smiled.

38
00:02:58.434 --> 00:03:01.894
"It's a book with a really good plot.

39
00:03:01.895 --> 00:03:06.682
In other words, exciting things happen to your main character."

40
00:03:06.683 --> 00:03:11.291
"Oh . . ." Colby nodded thoughtfully. "I see."

41
00:03:11.292 --> 00:03:17.130
Molly and I pushed our desks together so we could get started writing our book.

42
00:03:17.131 --> 00:03:19.682
First I tried to cheer up Molly.

43
00:03:19.683 --> 00:03:27.648
"I dreamed of a monster last night, but it was a funny monster," I told her.

44
00:03:27.649 --> 00:03:31.794
I drew a picture of the funny monster from my dream.

45
00:03:31.795 --> 00:03:34.331
Molly didn't laugh though.

46
00:03:34.332 --> 00:03:36.127
Not even a little.

47
00:03:36.128 --> 00:03:41.428
"My monsters aren't funny," she said.

48
00:03:41.429 --> 00:03:44.890
"This afternoon I'm going to try to distract Caswell.

49
00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:46.422
I'll make him popcorn.

50
00:03:46.423 --> 00:03:50.686
Then maybe he'll forget about watching Monster Madness."

51
00:03:50.687 --> 00:03:53.097
"Iggy and Molly, do you need help?"

52
00:03:53.098 --> 00:03:56.537
asked Mrs. Romano, coming over to us.

53
00:03:56.538 --> 00:03:58.818
"No," I said.

54
00:03:58.819 --> 00:04:02.516
"We just need to think of a plot for a story."

55
00:04:02.517 --> 00:04:06.912
"Why don't you brainstorm?" suggested Mrs. Romano.

56
00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:12.275
"Brainstorm" means you think of lots of ideas as fast as you can.

57
00:04:12.276 --> 00:04:18.978
We tried to brainstorm, but we didn't come up with any fantastic ideas.

58
00:04:18.979 --> 00:04:23.301
All Molly could think about were scary monsters.

59
00:04:23.302 --> 00:04:28.311
My ideas were mostly about my room and how much I hated to clean it up.

60
00:04:28.312 --> 00:04:32.282
I wished I had a big machine to do all the work for me.

61
00:04:32.283 --> 00:04:38.612
At last I got a good idea.
